#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:5
#: 521cb804a4304f9bafe1dddc6a21fbc0
msgid "Updating the Bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:7
#: f13a52c5de3a4afe8d7a16032904fd7b
msgid "A Bootloader is a small piece of code that runs (normally just for a few seconds) when an autopilot is powered on.  One of the bootloader's primary responsibilities is to allow easy upgrading of the main firmware (i.e. ArduPilot)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:9
#: ec9768b1757a44f09a5f9fa24510c30a
msgid "Nearly all autopilots ship with a bootloader pre-installed and most users will never need to upgrade it but there are some advantages to upgrading to the latest ArduPilot specific bootloader:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:11
#: 2575dad063f249c38a428a7da6be80b4
msgid "Bug fixes like the \"Parameter Reset\" issue fix included with Copter-4.0.4, Plane-4.0.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:12
#: c0908829e10d4b8fadec95373e205f65
msgid "The COM port name may be more recognisable.  For example it may include \"ArduPilot\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:16
#: 3d649cb59df14ca8884cc7a3d72f1d10
msgid "Updating the bootloader can potentially \"brick\" the board (i.e. make it unresponsive and unable to upload new firmwares).  Be careful not to power down the autopilot during the update process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:19
#: d789388af11641679a2733f0fcf6f986
msgid "Where can I download the latest bootloader?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:21
#: 606022662e8f4202847fa795e0a8409b
msgid "The ArduPilot specific bootloader is included within the ArduPilot firmware but it lies dormant by default.  A special command must be sent to the main ArduPilot firmware to install the new bootloader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:26
#: df946cccba3d4c39a40f40ec83a202a1
msgid "some autopilots with 1MB of flash do NOT have the bootloader included to save flash and the following attempts to upgrade from the firmware will result in a failure message in Mission Planner or Mavproxy. In those cases, you will need to flash the ``xxxx_bl.hex`` firmware for the autopilot using DFU as explained in :ref:`common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards` as if it did not already have ArduPilot firmware loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:29
#: 72e5e9b4c64f403bbb36db27a9352c02
msgid "Upgrading using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:31
#: 64e05107727f4cc2b61ac6426e15d2eb
msgid "Install a recent version of ArduPilot to the autopilot (:ref:`with existing ArduPilot firmware <common-loading-firmware-onto-pixhawk>`, :ref:`without existing ArduPilot firmware <common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:32
#: 92f78c8d25af492794ba8deccf58c68a
msgid "Connect and check that the autopilot has at least 20k of free memory.  Open the Data screen's Quick tab, double click on any entry and the select \"freemem\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:37
#: cada63366c6c445b984a2c4add9538f3
msgid "Open the Setup >> Install Firmware page and press the \"Bootloader Update\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bootloader-update.rst:42
#: b48ade62ee1b427cb6f54156b5277f2a
msgid "Reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

